## Already implemented

Native Windows editor: .NET 10 WPF, C++20, FFmpeg decoding/encoding, D3D11 composition, WASAPI audio, shared preview/export timeline evaluation, rational rates and integer project frames. Original media stays unchanged. Editing includes grouped events, trim/move/split, locks, undo/redo, clipboard rate conversion, levels/fades, project recovery/relink and export.

Event Pan/Crop has source-pixel position/size, rotation/pivot, aspect lock, interactive source workspace, six temporal curves, right-click/keyboard curve selection, keyframe drag/exact retiming and undo. The editor preserves colliding key states on separate whole frames. The default domain retiming API can replace a destination; the UI opts into preservation. Spatial spline smoothing and masks are not implemented.

Latest completed commit before this pass: 76ee228 (keyframe curve menu). Previous local validation: 124 core + 29 media + 53 editor + 4 playback + 16 native + 1 desktop workflow = 227 passed; zero managed build warnings/errors. GitHub CI passed. These results apply to that completed version, not to new edits in this pass.

