## Working rules and validation

- Preserve existing work and open unsaved editor sessions. Do not replace an executable bundle while it is running. Use dist/OpenRend-next for the new development package when dist/OpenRend is in use.
- Run tools/build.ps1 for native and managed checks. Desktop checks require OPENREND_RUN_UI_TESTS=1 and an unlocked interactive desktop; use isolated OPENREND_DATA_DIR. To verify the packaged desktop, set OPENREND_APP_PATH to its executable.
- Package separately with tools/package.ps1 -OutputDirectory E:\OpenRend\dist\OpenRend-next. The default package destination is dist/OpenRend, so check running sessions before using it.
- Use concise comments for timing, ownership and non-obvious behavior. Stage explicit paths, make small truthful tested commits, and push to the configured GitHub remote as authorized. Never invent test results or commit history.
- Keep private investigation evidence, dependency SDKs and generated binaries outside commits. Public documentation describes OpenRend's own implementation and measured limits.
